# OverconvergentAutomorphicForms: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It states the roadmap's
headline theorems against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti APIs whenever their
carriers are available. None of the following headlines is statable at these pins:

* General finite-slope Jacquet admissibility and coherent character-space duality
  (Layer 0) lack locally analytic representation categories, full rigid character
  spaces and the finite-slope Jacquet construction.
* The geometric Hilbert coefficient construction, its algebraic specialization,
  and the geometric and arithmetic AIP comparisons (Layers 2–5) lack native
  perfectoid Hilbert towers, their Hodge–Tate frame torsors, AIP formal torsors,
  and the associated analytic and integral coefficient sheaves.
* Family Koecher extension, torsion boundary vanishing, Fourier injectivity and
  Hecke/AIP compatibility (Layer 6) lack Hilbert toroidal/minimal compactifications,
  analytic-family coefficient pushforwards and coefficient-valued expansions.
* The cuspidal Banach theorem and complete continuity of the Hilbert controlling
  operator (Layer 6) lack the overconvergent cuspidal Banach modules, their
  boundary pushforwards and geometric Hecke correspondences.
* The ordinary Igusa completion and weighted ordinary comparison (Layer 7) lack
  the level-indexed good-reduction and toroidal ordinary Igusa torsors, the anticanonical
  wild-level limits, and their formal function sheaves and analytic spectral
  completions with power-bounded models. Their ordinary boundary completion
  comparison also lacks toroidal-to-minimal pushforwards and the completed
  coefficient-valued cusp-unit invariant sheaves; a minimal Igusa torsor is
  not a carrier for this comparison.
* The definite unitary Jacquet eigenvariety's dimension, Cohen–Macaulay property
  and reducedness (Layer 0) lack completed automorphic coefficient functions,
  locally analytic Jacquet modules and rigid eigenvarieties.
* The Siegel analytic coefficient and algebraic comparisons (Layer 8) lack the
  Siegel period-domain tower and normalized analytic induction sheaves.
* The toroidal algebraic comparison and Bruhat coefficient/distribution
  cohomology comparison in all degrees (Layer 8) lack toroidal tower diamonds,
  reduced de Rham torsors, their analytic coefficient sheaves and the required
  analytic and étale coefficient cohomology carriers.

The elementary tensor, character, cocycle and matrix formulas specifying these
constructions are targets and Checks in README.md. They do not replace any of
these headline theorems here.
-/

